Category E: Foreign Runtime, Robotics & WebUI Security (High / Medium Severity)
Finding 5.1: Python Backend IPC & Desktop Automation Network Isolation
Severity: High
Affected Files:
src/Singularity/Foreign/py/app.py
src/Singularity/Foreign/py/api/
src/Singularity/Physical/py/robotics/
Root Cause: The Python foreign backend incorporates Flask, Flask-SocketIO, Playwright, and desktop control libraries (pyscreeze, mouseinfo, pygetwindow). If app.py is started with host 0.0.0.0 or deployed on a shared network without strict session token validation, external network clients could invoke foreign automation endpoints to control local cursor/keyboard operations or execute unauthorized Playwright browser sessions.
Impact: Potential unauthorized local or remote interface control.
Actionable Remediation:
Explicitly hardcode server binding to 127.0.0.1 (localhost loopback) in app.py and Run Earthcall Python.command.
Implement authorization token verification using the Earthcall Identity::Claim / KeyStore cryptographic ledger for all incoming WebSocket/REST control commands.
Validate and sanitize all file paths passed to foreign save/export endpoints to prevent path traversal.


Finding 5.2: Workspace Cleanliness & Git Untracked Directories
Severity: Low
Affected Directories:
agent intercom/robots having fun and messing around/
.gitignore (uncommitted modifications)
Actionable Remediation: Review and clean up temporary multi-agent scratch directories and commit updated ignore patterns to ensure clean workspace state.


